<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n61198" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κώδων</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ωνος</span><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">, ὁ</span> (
			Att.
		
		ἡ
		<i><span class="en">
			S.
			<u>Aj.</u>
			17
		</span></i>, dub. in <i><span class="en">
			Ar.
			<u>Pax</u>
			1078
		</span></i>), <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>bell</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπ᾽ ἀσπίδος δὲ τῷ χαλκήλατοι
					κλάζουσι κ. φόνον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Th.</u>
					386
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				399
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Rh.</u>
				308
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χαλκοστόμου κώδωνος ὡς
				Τυρσηνικῆς</span>, i.e. a trumpet, S.l.c. (where Sch. expl.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κώδων</span> as <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ πλατὺ τῆς σάλπιγγος</span>, i.e. the <i>mouth</i>
			of the trumpet, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Ath.
				5.185a
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Poll.
				2.203
			</span></i>); carried on rounds of inspection to challenge sentries, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοῦ κώδωνος πα ενεχθέντος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Th.
					4.135
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐφοδεύειν κώδωνι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					<u>Arat.</u>
					7
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Merc.Cond.</u>
				24
			</span></i>, Sch.<i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Av.</u>
				843
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>crier's bell</i>, hence <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ταῦθ᾽ οὗτος
				μόνον οὐ κώδωνας ἐξαψάμενος διαπράττεται</span> 'is his
			own trumpeter', <i><span class="en">
				D.
				25.90
			</span></i>: metaph., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ κ. ἀκαλανθίς
				</span>(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὅτι λάλον τὸ
			ζῷον</span> Sch.) <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Pax</u>
				1078
			</span></i> (perh. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κύων</span> is the true
			reading, v.
			<i><span class="en">
				<u>App. Prov.</u>
				1.12
			</span></i>); cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κρόταλον</span>.
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κωδύα, τῆς μήκωνος</span>
			
			<i><span class="en">
				Dieuch.
			</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
				Orib.
				4.6.2
			</span></i>.</div>
